1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Canada has seven glaciers that scientists have measured for more than 40 years.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,800
All seven have shrunk. Take Peyto Glacier, in Alberta. In its first 35 years, it lost 18 metres.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,300
Then came 2023. Helm Glacier lost 4.4 metres in one year. Its worst year on record.

4
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:19,400
Place Glacier, worst year. Peyto, worst year.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,300
So Peyto's next 25 years? 30 metres. More than the 35 years before.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,000
Faster, is what I'm getting at.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,900
Since 1966, Peyto's down 48 and a half metres.

8
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,300
Seven for seven. Not a streak you want.

